abstract: Xi yi ju yu [Gleanings of Western medicine] is John Dudgeon’s collection of medical articles from
  Zhong xi wen jian lu, catalogued as 1875 [Peking] and held as Bodleian Sinica 1842. Its five prefaces and
  illustrated essays on the heart, circulation, eyes, and forensic medicine support research on late Qing medical
  history, translation, and publishing. This release offers JSON, TXT, and TEI transcriptions across 161 source
  positions with notes, labels, tables, and source links. Historical vaccination instructions at c060 left,
  c061–c074 and c075 right are outside its coverage. The AI-assisted transcription marks uncertain readings
  and awaits full human collation.
